# 0011. Test the config with a headless make check that captures vim.notify

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-11

## Context
lazy.nvim and plugins report errors through `vim.notify`, which prints nothing with `--headless`.
A plain `nvim --headless +qa` passed with a broken lazy-loaded plugin.

## Decision
`make check` runs (1) a plain headless start, then (2) `scripts/check.lua`, which captures
`vim.notify`, loads every plugin and opens one file per language. Any error fails it.
`make startup` times five starts against the budget in [0002](0002-lazy-nvim-pinned-and-lazy-loaded.adr).

## Alternatives
- Plain headless start: misses errors, as above.

## Rationale
Catches broken plugins before they reach `main` and every machine.

## Consequences
- New languages or plugins should be covered by `scripts/check.lua`.

## References
- `Makefile`, `scripts/check.lua`, PR #2
